; Complete programs from the guides, compiled with everything else so the
; pages that quote them cannot drift from the engine: room.ml is step 1 of
; making-a-game (and README.md's example), doorways.ml is step 5, game.ml is
; step 12 and rebind.ml is step 13. Attached to no package, so nothing
; installs them and the -p builds opam runs never see them.

(executables
 (names room doorways game rebind)
 (modules room doorways game rebind)
 (libraries camlcast))

; The declarative layer's own, kept beside its counterpart on purpose:
; described_room.ml is room.ml said the other way, and test_stage renders the
; two and compares every pixel. A stanza of its own because it is the only one
; here that needs camlcast.stage.

(executables
 (names described_room)
 (modules described_room)
 (libraries camlcast camlcast_stage))
